# Post-mortem -- slice 0252, attempt 01

## Summary

Slice 0252 (the S8.1 run law) is complete and judged green on its merits. It cannot pass its ui-tests gate because the selected class InverseConstructorTests carries a deterministic red that step 0227 committed and nobody was authorized to repair.
The red is `recommitting a copied experiment preserves its assigned physical ids`. The judge escalated at cycle 1 and the resolver confirmed, because the repair is a fixture edit in `InverseConstructorTests.fs`, outside 0252's authorized effects. Only an operator ruling can grant that authority.

## Root cause

Owner: **the product**, as it stood before the slice. The failing fact (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs:458-527`, written at step 0221, last changed in `673ae0e`) simulates a copied experiment. It assigns three hard-coded `ItemId`s (`pieceA` `3c9e1f47-…`, `pieceB`, `samplePiece`, lines 473-476) and writes only the experiment (`writeExperiment`, line 491), never the items. Step 0227 (`6cb35e2`, the only commit that introduced `Experiment.itemsUsedBy [ experiment ] items` into `KitContentFiles.fs`) made `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` (`KitContentFiles.fs:203-210`) refuse an assigned id the kit does not hold, before writing. `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` (`Experiments.fs:294-308`) checks only that the id exists. The fact's recommit therefore goes through `ExpCommit` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2477-2505`) to `recordExperiment` and on to `UnknownKitItemErr`. That sets `kitStatus` to "Not saved to the kit — the items could not be copied: the kit has no item of that id: 3c9e1f47-…", and the `None` assertion at line 509 fails.

A real copy can never produce that state. Since 0227, `copyExperimentsFrom` writes every added item before the experiments. The fixture is stale against the 0227 contract, and the product refusal is correct. Changing the product to accept unknown ids would reverse 0227's deliberate pre-write guard, so that option is dropped. The 0252 diff never reaches this path (no `recordExperiment`, `ExpCommit`, `itemIdOpt` or `kitStatus` line in its hunks).

Three tool-side contributors let the red reach this slice.
- **The selection at 0227.** The ledger's gate plan for step 0227 (`.spec-jsonl` line 227, `gate_selection.ui-tests` = KitWindowTests and ExperimentControlsTests) omitted the class that pins the changed record path, so 0227 went green over it. 0227 is completed and frozen, and standing ruling 2 forbids amending the ledger.
- **The silent note at 0242.** The 0242 worker and judge both found the red, reproduced it on an unmodified HEAD, and passed `review-green` with only a prose note (`code_judge/0242-01-code-judge.md:75-82`).
- **The wrong forward pointer.** That note said "before step 0261 selects that class", but 0252 is the first step that selects it.

No notification fired at 0242: NOTIFY-POSTED appears in the log only with the 17 ESCALATION-RECORDED events. No provider or model change is implicated: implement_worker, code_judge, resolver and postmortem have all been anthropic `claude-opus-5-5[1m]` since step 0160.

This is a **repeat of a recorded class**. The 0185 review (`0185-01.postmortem-review-md:131-133`) named it: "an accepted fixture affected by later behavior but omitted from that later step's edit authority". 0150 was the sibling case, inherited warnings from 0146-0147. Manual 014 deliberately granted specific authority only ("not a general permission"), so no class fix exists. This case differs in one way: because 0227's selection omitted the class, the red surfaced 25 steps later, in an unrelated step.

